You do not need to demonize the people of Khabarovsk
The acting head of the Khabarovsk Krai spoke about his trip to the region in an exclusive interview with Komsomolskaya Pravda
Acting Governor of the Khabarovsk Territory Mikhail Degtyarev called in an interview the observer of “Komsomolskaya Pravda” Alexander Gamova does not demonize Khabarovsk citizens against the background of rallies in support of the arrested ex-head of the region Sergey Furgal.
I want to appeal to all political commentators, political scientists, participants of any talk shows.
Do not deprompize the people of the Khabarovsk region.
Here live hard-loving and wonderful people, - said Mikhail Degtyarev.
In an interview, Degtyarev recalled that he is a member of the LDPR and a member of Furgal and added that he wishes him good luck in the court, and Vladimir Zhirinovsky personally will provide support in the court.
The full text of the interview is published on the website of KP.ru.
Earlier, the website of KP.ru reported that Mikhail Degtyarev called for an open trial of Sergei Furgal and considers it fair to hold it in Khabarovsk.
In the two Mexican states declared an Albitude due to Hurricane Hannah
The U.S. National Civil Defense Authority has declared an “orange” (tough) level of anxiety in the two eastern states of Tamaulipas and Nuevo León due to Hurricane Hannah, TASS reported.
Hurricane will bring heavy downpours to Mexika, in some areas they predict the loss of 150 to 250 liters of precipitation per square meter.
The authorities have prepared about 800 sanctuaries for the population.
To provide assistance to the people will be 10 thousand people, including rescuers, soldiers of the national guard and the military.
At the moment, the hurricane has reached the coast of the American state of Texas with a wind speed of 150 km / h.
Hannah’s arrival in Mexico is expected on Sunday morning.
Semilarsky against the Prosecutor’s office: the cassation of the former vice-mayor of Tartu will be considered on August 4
This means that the decision on it will most likely be made in early September.
The courts of the first two instances to consider Semiralski's claim, but in April his cassation appeal was accepted by the State Court.
The Tartu administrative court on December 12, 2019 returned the complaint to the applicant, since its permission does not fall within its competence of an administrative court.
In the court order it was stated that the complaint contains a claim for the reparations caused in the course of a criminal proceeding.
“Regulate such issues, the Prosecutor’s office and the county’s judicial court should be regulated,” Anette Kreitsmann, a spokeswoman of the Tartu Vessels, said.
According to her, Valvo Semilarski appealed this decision to the district court, which on February 5 did not change the decision of the court of first instance.
Now it will have to say its word to the State court.
According to Semilarsky’s defender Oliver Nääs, his client was unreasonably suspected of bribe-taking for about two years unreasonably.
Now he is desunicing from the prosecutor's office to refute the wrong statements in his address and compensate him for the moral damage.
The reason for filing a complaint with the court was the statements of the Prosecutor for special cases of the Lyuna district Prosecutor’s office Margus Gross, made by him in October 2017, when Semilarsky, along with another vice-mayor of Tartu at that time, Artem Suvorov, was detained on suspicion of committing several crimes.
“Responsible that when I was detained, the Security Police and the Prosecutor’s Office immediately organized a press conference and informed the whole of the Estonian Republic that the leaders of Tartu - one of the most influential bodies of the local arbitrariñals - are venal.
These hovering in the air public suspicion accompanied me for about two years.
And now, when these statements and suspicions turned out to be false, the prosecutor's office does not want to say anything about it," Sémilarski said in early August 2019.
According to Oliver Nyaez, at the press conference, the prosecutor went beyond the legal framework in which the Prosecutor’s office should operate.
“Receipts and venal claims turned out to be flawed, but this is not the only problem here.
The European Court of Human Eprdom, for example, has repeatedly stressed in their rulings on Russia, as well as in Lithuania that at the investigative stage, state representatives should be careful when selecting words so that the suspects would not be presented in the role of criminals prior to sentencing.
To this the prosecutor's office obliges the presumption of innocence, which, unfortunately, has not been complied with in this case against Valvo Semilarsky," Nääs said.
“Semilarsky’s public presentation as a serious offender and a bribe-taker in the circumstances, where the facts underlying suspicion of bribery are still being ascertained is inadmissible, which continually continuors the presumption of innocence and is unfair to the claimant,” the lawyer said.
According to rus.err.ee the former vice-mayor of Tartu Valvo Semiralski will not be prosecuted on charges of sceniorblowing - a criminal case against him was partially closed in July.
At the same time, the former official is judged on charges of deliberately violating anti-corrupt legislation when conducting transactions on an especially large scale.
According to an incremental conclusion, between 2015 and 2017, the former Deputy Mayor of Tartu more than thirty times participated in the meetings of the city government when making decisions associated with companies operating in Tartu, with the owners or the heads of which Semilarsky actively communicated at a personal level at an out-of-the-hour.
According to Gross, in all of these cases Semilarsky had personal interests, and therefore he had to distance himself from participating in decision-making.
Earlier, as rus.err.ee wrote, the Prosecutor’s office susciful presented Semilarski about receiving a bribe and violating the anti-corruption legislation when carrying out transactions on an especially large scale.
This happened in October 2016, when he was detained along with another deputy mayor Artem Suvorov (Centrist Party).
Then the Prosecutor’s office and the security police stated that there is strong evidence against both vice-ma-mayors.
After that, both officials resigned.
Suvorov’s case later reached the court, which completely acquitted the politician.
Judgment in Valvo Semilarski is still ongoing.
