In St. Petersburg ended the main naval parade in honor of the Day of the Navy
Kronstadt’s main naval parade ended, dedicated to celebrating the Russian Naval Day.
According to RIA Novosti, the military review took place with a small gathering of spectators.
In connection with preventive measures to prevent the spread of the coronavirus to the parade, it was possible to get only on passes.
In the main naval parade in St. Petersburg and Kronstadt were attended by 46 ships, including patrol "Vasily Bykov" and the anti-submarine "Vice-Admiral Kulakov".
Various batters and submarines, aircraft and helicopters of naval aviation and about four thousand servicemen were also involved.
In Kronstadt on the occasion of celebrating the Day of the Naval arrived the supreme commander-in-chief of the Armed forces of the Russian Federation, President Vladimir Putin.
He bypassed the ceremonial thirsty of warships in the Gulf of Finland and the Kronstadt Raid.
Congratulated the servicemen on the holiday, marking the unique advantages and increasing the combat capabilities of the Russian fleet.
According to the Russian leader, the level of equipment of the Russian Navy is constantly growing, so, this year 40 ships and vessels of various classes will be accepted into its composition.
naval parades on the Day of the Navy were held at bases in Balt, Vladivostok, Severomorsk, Sevastopol and Kaspiyssk.
