two more highways are included in the list of federal roads
The government of the Russian Federation has included two more highways in the list of federal roads.
According to Kabmin, one of these roads more than 663 kilometers Chekshino - Totma - Kotla - Kuratovo connects the Vologda and Arkhangelsk regions with the Republic of Komi.
The other highway more than 388-kilometres leads from Barnaul through Pavlovsk to the border with the Republic of Kazakhstan.
On this road you can pass from the capital of the Altai region to the Kulund checkpoint.
Receiving a new status will lead these routes to a normative state at the expense of the Federal Road Fund.
Overhaul will be carried out and the reconstruction of certain areas, the quality of the road surface will be improved.
