On Sunday, parades in honor of the Russian Naval Naval Day took place in St. Petersburg and next to all major naval bases, including the Syrian Tartus.
They were attended by 219 different ships and 15 thousand personnel.
The President of Russia Vladimir Putin, who took the main parade in St. Petersburg, said that in 2020 the composition of the Navy will be replenished with 40 new ships of different classes, as well as the latest weapons - including hypersonic strike complexes and unmanned underwater vehicles.
In 2020, the parade for the first time was held in Kaspiyssk, where the Caspian fleet base was redeploydated from Astrakhan.
In addition to St. Petersburg, the parades were held in Balt, Kaspiysk, Severomorsk, Petropavlovsk-Kamchatsky, Vladivostok, as well as in an annexed Sevastopol and on the Raid Raid of the Syrian port of Tartus.
In the main parade, 4 thousand soldiers and 46 vessels, including nuclear and diesel submarines took part, including nuclear and diesel submarines, as well as helicopter helicopters and naval aviation.
At the beginning of the parade, Putin, accompanied by Defense Minister Sergei Shoigu, commander-in-Chief of the Naims, Admiral Nikolai Yevmènov and the commander of the troops of the Western Military District, Colonel-General Zhuravlev bypassed several ships standing on the Kronshtade Rada and in the Gulf of Finland, greeting the personnel.
Decoration of the parade was a copy of the first Russian battleship "Poltava", reconstituted according to archival drawings.
In its design was attended by the Emperor Peter I.
In his speech, Putin recalled that this year marks the 200-anniversary of the discovery of Antarctica as a result of an expedition of Russian navigators Fadday Bellingshausen and Mikhail Lazarev.
Snipers who ensured safety were seen on the roof of the Senate and Synode building during the parade during the parade.
More than 46 warships and more than 1.5 soldiers took part in the parade in Baltiysk, where the Baltic Fleet is based, and a large Kaliningrad warship has landed amphibious assault.
In the annexed Sevastopol parad, a parade was held with the participation of 30 ships and a performance dedicated to the history of the Black Sea Fleet, which also included the exit of a group of divers from under the water.
In the parade in Severomorsk involved a new nuclear submarine "Prince Vladimir" of strategic purpose, accepted as part of the Northern Fleet in June.
In Vladivostok the feast ended with a salute.
The NAW of the Russian Federation this year will receive forty ships and ships
Forty ships and vessels will be replenished this year by the composition of the Russian nam, said Russian President Vladimir Putin.
“Environment of equipment of our navy is constantly growing.
This year will be accepted forty ships and vessels of various classes,” he said, speaking at the main parade in honor of the day of the Navy in St. Petersburg.
Putin also recalled that a few days ago at three shipyards in Russia there were six more new ships of the far sea zone.
Earlier it was reported that in St. Petersburg began a parade in honor of the Day of the Navy.
