The officers of the Northern Fleet received state awards
The commander of the Northern Fleet Hero of Russia Vice-Admiral Alexander Moiseyev presented state awards to distinguished officers.
This is stated in the message on the official website of the Ministry of Defense.
As noted in the report, 12 senior and senior officers from the underwater forces, army corps, air and air defense armies, the White Sea Naval base, units of weapons and the headquarters of the Northern Fleet received the orders and medals.
Rear-Admiror Sergei Grishko, the head of the technical department of the Northern Fleet, was thanked by the President of the Russian Federation.
How the decision of the Central Bank to reduce the key rate will affect the economy
The Bank of Russia is expected to again reduce the key rate.
It fell by another 0.25 percentage points, to 4.25% per anniversaries - formally another historical minimum.
Judging by the return of a short step of lowering the rates, as well as the tonality of CSB's statements and updated forecasts for the Russian economy, the regulator is looking at economic prospects more optimistically than before.
This means that the current monetary easing cycle may soon stop.
“We continued to easing the monetary policy, primarily taking into account that there are still risks of deviating inflation from 4% in 2021”, – said the head of the Bank of Russia Elvira Nabiullina.
They are connected with a significant decrease in economic activity, a drop in internal and external demand.
The restoration of the economy, according to Nabiullina, will take more than a year and a half.
At the same time, she noted that after the lifting of restrictions due to the pandemic, economic processes revived: energy consumption, consumer and investment demand were recovered, the construction and production of consumer goods were expanded, the annual rate of decrease in the cargo turnover of transport and industrial production decreased.
According to the updated forecast of the Central Bank, in 2020 the contraction of the economy will amount to 4.5-5.5% (before it was expected 4-6%), and the economic recovery growth in 2021 will amount to 3.5-4.5%, in 2022 - 2.5-3.
In addition, the Bank of Russia has revised the forecast for annual oil prices of up to $ 38 and $ 40 per barrel of Urals in 2020 and 2021, respectively.
Earlier, the Central Bank waited for $ 27 and $ 35 per barrel.
Finally, the forecast of the Bank of Russia on inflation for 2020 amounted to 3.7-4.2% against the previously expected 3.8-4.8%.
The opinion of the Bank of Russia about the situation in the economy is becoming more optimistic, which brings us closer to the end of the easing cycle, economists in Russia and the CIS “Renaissance Capital” Sophia Donets and Andriy Melashchenko said.
So, the Bank of Russia has consistently reduced the key rate for more than a year, since the beginning of last summer it has already dropped by 3.5 percentage points.
And at the last meeting in June, the Central Bank lowered it at once by one percentage point due to low rates of inflation in connection with reduced demand and the need to spur the economy that has stifled because of the pandemic and the associated restrictions.
Opportunities for the adjustment of the monetary policy are preserved (at the next meeting on September 18 until the end of the year), but the limit is already close, agrees the chief analyst of Rosbank Evgeny Koshelev.
The combination of pro-inflationary risks also points to pause pause in easing interest policies - disrupted supply chains, a possible increase in costs due to measures to prevent an epidemic (compared compared to expectations) recovery of demand, he says.
To overcome the subsequent actions of the Bank of Russia will require more attention to the inflationary processes during the helm season, as well as external volatility that has increased against the background of geopolitical conflicts, Koshelev points.
In one way or another, the reduction of the key rate will lead to a further reduction in rates for the most reliable borrowers, as well as, possibly on a mortgage, senior economist of the analytical department of Otkritie Bank Maxim Petronevich.
Correction of bets will be a less pronounced nature than a reduction in the key rate, he clarifies.
Bets on consumer loans can fall by another 0.3-0.6 percentage points during the second half of the year, mortgage rates can end the year in the range of 6.2-7%, Anton Pokatovich does not rule.
The average interest rates on deposits, in his opinion, will also fall - in the coming months they can fall to 4.2-4.5% (now just above 4.5%).
Then they can fall to 4%, if the Central Bank reduces the key rate in the fall, Pokatovich said.
