The main naval parade, consisting of 46 warships, boats and submarines, 41 planes and a helicopter of naval aviation and more than 4 thousand servicemen ended in Kronstadt.
In the parade, in particular, involved a large anti-submarine ship "Vice-Admiral Kulakov", corvette "Stable", large amphibious landing ships "Minsk" and "Patriot", the nuclear underwater missile cruiser "Eagle", the underwater boat "Petropavlovsk-Kamchatsky", a patrol ship "Vasily Bykov", a small anti-serk.
On Kronstadt Raid in the Gulf of Finland, you could first see a large amphibious landing ship "Peter Morgunov", built according to the project 11711 of the Nevsky PCB at the Baltiysk Yantar plant.
The main ship of this series "Ivan Gren" is already serving in the Northern fleet, reports TASS.
Among other beginners who recently came into service with the NAW, was the first serial frigate "Admiral Kasatonov fleet", built according to the project 22350 at the plant "Northern shipyard".
Another novice of the NAV - diesel-electric submarine "Petropavlovsk-Kamchatsky" project 636.3 of the Central Design Bureau of marine technology "Rubin", built at the "Admiralty shipyards".
It rejossengthened Russia’s Pacific Fleet in December 2019.
The other newest ships, recently included in the NAV - small rocket ships "Sovetsk" and "Mytishchi" of project 22800 ("Karakurt"), developed by TsMKB "Almaz".
In the parade on the Neva also involved small missile ships "Verily Ustyug" and "Serpukhov" project 21631 "Buyan-M".
And the largest participants were the nuclear underwater missile crutak "Orel" and a large anti-submarine ship "Vice-Admiral Kulakov" - they could be seen in the Gulf of Finland.
In recognition of a large contribution of the Russian fleet to the study of the World Ocean, together with warships on the Neva passed two new hydrographic boats "George Winter" and "Mikhail Kazansky". And on the Kronstadt Raid, an oceanographic research vessel "Admiral Vladimirsky", which in June completed a joint with the Russian geographical society a scientific round-twentily expedition.
And at the Palace bridge you could see the first Russian battleship "Poltava", recreated at a historic ship.
This 54-gun cloak was launched in 1712, participated in the Swedes, and in 1717 ensured the landing on the island of Gothland.
In 1725, this ship was withdrawn from Baltflot, and after its re-creation - was launched in St. Petersburg on May 27, 2018.
Travel to Kronstadt this year was limited during the parade in connection with the prevention of the spread of the coronavirus COVID-19, reports RIA Novosti.
