Unnecessary requirements for applications for public procurement will be eliminated by law
In the legislation can establish comprehensive requirements for applications for participation in the procurement.
In the Autumn session at a plenary meeting of the state Duma plan to consider in the second reading a bill that establishes the requirements for the content and composition of the application for participation in the procurement, the participants of which can be only small and medium-sized businesses.
Modification is submitted by the government to the law "On Proceedings of Commodities, Work and Services by certain types of legal entities".
The bill has been developed in compliance with the roadmap for the implementation of the Strategy for the development of small and medium-sized entrepreneurship in the RUSSIAN RUSSIAN until 2030, approved by the government.
It stipulates the preparation of a draft of the law on an exhaustive list of documents, which the customers have the right to demand as part of an application from purchasing participants - small and medium-sized businesses.
As well as the list of requirements for these documents.
To this day in the law “On the procurement of goods, works and services by certain types of legal entities”, the framework regulates the procurement activities of certain types of legal entities.
The requirements for the content, form, registration and composition of the application for participation in the procurement shall be established by the customers independently in the documentation of the purchase.
As a result, customers are establishing redundant requirements for the content, registration of an application, the mandatory presence of certificates, certificates, certificates, statements, the period of receipt of which in the authorized bodies is comparable with the deadline for submitting applications, which leads to the impossimilation of participation in such a procreation and a reduction in the number of participants in the procurement”, – stated in the Expenditure to the bill.
The new bill stipulates the establishment of a comprehensive list of documents that customers have the right to demand as part of an application from procurement participants who are small and medium-sized businesses.
“The adoption of the document will allow you to exclude an arbitrari imitative establishment by customers of the requirements for the composition and content of applications of participants who are small and medium-sized businesses,” the explanatory note reads.
