In China on the Yangtze river there was the third in a year of floating
After a powerful downpour in the upper reaches of the Yangtze River - the longest aquatic aquatic artery of China - for the third time in a year, floods appeared.
Flooding was caused by an increase in the water level in the tributaries of the river in its upper reaches, which led to a rapid increase in the flow of water to the reservoir of the Chinese Hansy hydroelectric power plant.
At 14:00 on July 26 there was an influx of 50 thousand cubic m / s in the reservoir, which is expected to reach its maximum in the evening of July 27 - 60 thousand cubic m / s, the Yangtze River's Water Management Committee said.
The Committee today issued notifications about the floats on one of the sections of the upper Yangtze river and overcrowding the reservoir of the Hansya hydroelectric power plant.
