The head of the region Igor Kobzev met with the mayors of the Ust-Orda Buryatsky district
During the working meeting, which took place today, July 24, in the government of the Irkutsk region discussed the main directions for the development of remote agrarian territories.
During working trips in the districts of the Ust-Horda Buryat district, the head of the region gave a number of instructions.
The mayors today reported their execution.
First of all resumed the construction of the House of sports in Ust-Orda.
Instruction on this object was given by the President of the Russian Federation fourteen years ago.
But only now the situation managed to move from a dead point.
866 million roubles will be spent on the construction.
Term of completion of the building in 2022 year.
And this year should be put into operation a school in the village of Bayandai.
At the moment the decoration of the premises has been completed.
Of the remaining works - the improvement of the territory.
In general, the program for the construction of pre-school and secondary educational facilities is of particular importance for the region.
For your district, in particular.
Demographic situation here is the best in the region.
And we are obliged to create all the conditions for the education and leisure of children of all ages, – said the acting Governor of the Irkutsk region Igor Kobzev.
At the meeting, the head of the region gave instructions to all the mayors to be actively involved in the work on the development of general plans of settlements.
This is one of the main conditions for the complex development of the district.
All human settlements must have established boundaries and a master plan.
This is necessary for the development of the territory, for the construction of socially significant objects, as well as objects of infrastructure and cultural heritage, – said the head of the region.
Also during the conversation, a problematic issue was raised with a reduction in the intake of milk from cooperatives by 30%.
This was due to the redistribution by the processing enterprise of the purchase of milk in favor of peasant farms.
Because of this, the share of receiving products from cooperatives has decreased.
The head of the region instructed the Acting Minister of agriculture to go to the place, to study the implementation of milk, to analyze the experience of other territories and to identify options for solving the problem.
