The authorities of the Moscow region told about the fate of closed landfill
In the Suburban region continue to close landfills of solid household waste.
This year, the authorities promise to liquidate the latter.
Some of the 39 existing landfills will be upgraded to modern garbage processing complexes.
But such an option is possible not for each landfill - many of them are overgrown with dense residential buildings.
After the polygon is closed, it stands for reclamation - the body of the polygon is sprinkled with soils, degassing and infiltrate withdrawal systems are mounted.
This allows you to stop the chemical processes inside the landfill so that it does not ignite inflamed, does not exude stalk, does not poison the soil and groundwater.
And then the former landfill remains to protrude a fusible bunch of residential buildings that surrounded her.
Why don’t you do anything useful out of it?
For example, in Rúz, where just the other day the reclamation of Annino landfill was completed, the authorities are considering an option to make a pile of a ski slope.
This training ground, operated from 1976 to 2016, grew so that it went beyond the land allocated to it.
Therefore, during rectivation it was necessary to repurchase the neighboring plots, the de facto have long been crumpled with garbage.
“For a while will pass, the polygon “sake”, there will be fortresses, and we will think what can be done so that it will begin to benefit.
Directly catches the eye - a ski resort, "- told reporters the head of the Ruzsky district Nikolay Parfenov.
Two polygons will become sites for the extraction of renewable energy
Sea ranges "Torbeevo" in Lyubertsy and "Tymochovo" in the Bogorodsky district will become platforms for the extraction of renewable energy sources from landfill and biological gases.
By the end of the year will be a gas pisting power plant that can produce up to 8 million kilowatt-hours of electricity and about 0.95 gigacalories of thermal energy per year, which will provide its own needs of the landfill - the heat of administrative and industrial premises.
"Timohovoo" will produce 72.5 million kilowatt-hours and will continue to operate as a garbage processing complex.
And at the Balashikha polygon Kuchino, which was closed after the complaints of the residents on "Straight line" with the President of the country, a museum can be created.
"There was such an idea - to create a museum of reclamation of polygons of the Moscow region", - said the deputy representative of the government - the minister of ecology and environmental management of the region Dmitry Kurakin.
