The Presidents of Russia and Ukraine discussed the implementation of the truce in the Donbass
The President of Russia Vladimir Putin and the President of Ukraine Volodymyr Zelensky discussed the implementation of agreements on a truce in the Donbas achieved during the Normandy summit in December 2019, the press service of the Kremlin and the office of the President of Ukraine reported.
The telephone conversation of Vladimir Putin and Vladimir Zelensky took place at the initiative of the Ukrainian side, according to the press service of the Kremlin.
The interlocutors welcomed the achievement on July 22 at the meeting of the Minsk Contact Group of an agreement on a complete and comprehensive ceasefire in the Donbas, which begins at 00:01 on July 27, 2020; the Russian President supported this agreement.
The leaders agreed on the need to urgently implement additional measures to support the ceasefire in the Donbas.
At the Same time, Putin criticized the decree adopted by the Verkhovna Verkhovna Rada on the organization of local elections in the state in the autumn, which, in the opinion of the Russian side, is ignoring the Minsk agreement.
The situation in connection with the coronavirus pandemic was also discussed.
On July 22, an agreement stipulates a complete renunciation of any hostilities, including reconnaissance, reconnaissance and sniper warfare.
