Putin arrived in St. Petersburg for the main parade of the NAV of the Russian Navy
The President on the boat went to the ceremonial failiation of ships in the Gulf of Finland
The President of Russia Vladimir Putin arrived in St. Petersburg for the main parade of the Russian Naval Naval.
He went on a clairbone to the ceremonial faucet of ships in the Gulf of Finland.
The parade in Kronstadt will be attended by 15 ships and submarines.
Including the patrol ship "Vasily Bykov", the oceanographic research vessel "Admiral Vladimirsky", the nuclear undercarriage missile-bearing cruising "Eagle", corvette "Stable", large amphibious assault ships "Minsk", "Peter Morgunov", "Korol" and a large anti-subscold ship "Vice-Admiral Kulakov".
After the Kronstadt parad, Putin will receive the main naval parade in the water area of the Neva.
The exposition in honor of the Day of the Navy was opened in the regional local lolaring museum
The exposition in honor of the Day of the Naval Fleet of Russia was opened in the Murmansk regional museum of local lore.
The exhibition is devoted to the history of the life of the admiral fleet of the Soviet Union Nikolay Kuznetsov.
In the exposition there are photographs, documents, posters and paintings from the life of the ill-glorified naval commander.
the decision to enlarge RPL would not have been upheld by either UEFA or FIFA
The President of the Russian football Union (RFU) Alexander Dyukov believes that it is not wrong to expand the Russian Premier League (RPL) to 18 teams at the moment.
“At first, it was the RPL decision, but I will acknowledge them, because it is wrong to change the rules after the tournament has been completed.
This is implication of the integrity of the tournament and the sports principle.
And, of course, this decision would not have been supported by either UEFA or FIFA," Dyukov Said after Zenith - Khimki (1:0).
At the present time in the RPL there are 16 clubs, but an option was being considered with an increase in the number of teams to 18.
more than a hundred Russians returned from Yerevan to their homeland with export flights
More than a hundred Russians, who could not leave Armenia against the background of the spread of the coronavirus, returned to their homeland with export flights.
About it on Sunday, July 26, was reported in the press service of the Russian Embassy in Yerevan.
“We are delighted to inform you that on July 26 with flights of Yereving – Rostov-on-Dun they were able to return to 106 Russians”, – quotes the message of TASS.
The Embassy noted that the process of registering and boarding passengers on the flight was coordinated by diplomats.
In total, since the imposition of restrictions on flights from Armenia, 2822 citizens of Russia have been withdrawn.
At the same time, on July 24, Russian Prime Minister Mikhail Mishustin said about the opening of air links with a number of countries from August 1.
Kirilenko shared memories of games with Bryant and Jórdan in the NBA
The head of the Russian Basketball Federation (RFB) Andrey Kirilenko shared his memorties about his games against the legendary Kobe Bryant and Michael Giordan in the matches of the National Basketball Association (NBA).
I knew Bryant couldn't be messed up with any trash, so I wouldn't encourage his athletic majesty.
Kobe had a killer's institute, so I've been trying to talk like he wouldn't take an aggressive game.
On the set, I complimented him: "Oh!
Kobe, you've scored well, a great passage!
Listening to my enthusiastic responses, he forgot a little bit that it is necessary to once again take the ball in his hands and score another 3 - 4 points.
We communicated well with Kobe,” Kirilenko quotes “Evening Moscow”.
He also spoke about his first game against Jordan.
"I carved him.
The first three minutes of the match I was completely admirable of the fact that next to me is a legend I, which I saw only on TV.
As long as I'm happy in the gonds, Michael scored a lot of points.
Soon I stepped away from excitement, a couple of times covered his shots ...
In this game, my team won, and Giordan still scored 44 points”, – said the head of the RFB.
Kirilenko in the NBA spent 12 seasons.
He was selected by Utah Jazz in the 1999 draft at number 24.
In addition to “Yuhuta”, for which he spent ten seasons, the Russian striker played for “Minnesota Timburwells” and “Bruckline Nets”.
In total, on his account of 797 matches, in which on average he scored an average of 11.8 points, performed 5.5 rebounds, 2,7 assistants and 1.8 block shots.
Earlier it was reported that Kirylenko will nominate his candidacy for the election of the head of the RFB.
Degtyarev was amazed by the information about the purchase of Sakhalin-1 for dollars
The acting Governor of the Khabarovsk Territory, Mikhail Degtyarev on Sunday, July 26, during a meeting with the residents of Sovet Havana was amazed that the region is buying Sakhalin gas, extracted by the American company Exxon Neftegas for dollars.
U.S. gas has been contracted in dollars until 2025.
Honestly, I didn't know that, and I'm at such a knockdown because of this information.
I did not even have an idea that this is still possible in 2020 in Russia”, – quotes him “RIA Novosti”.
Degtyarev noted that this issue was discussed with the head of the Ministry of Energy of Russia Alexander Novak during his visit to Khabarovsk on July 14.
The acting governor also stressed that by 2025 “Gazprom” is switching to the supply of Russian thermal power plants and capacities, which means that Russian gas will be used, purchased in ruble “at normal prices”.
Sakhalin-1 project is being implemented through a product-sharing agreement, where Exxon Neftegas Ltd is the project operator with a share of 30%, another 20% from Rosneft, and the Japanese Sodeco has a 30% stake and the Indian ONGC has 20%.
Khabarovsk Krai has been acquiring gas from this project since 2005.
